 "node_degree", "args": {"nodes": [389, 987, 1299, 92, 1446, 1378], "window": [5632, 44032]}, "result_digest": "e516d2d9cd346770", "result_summary": "{\"nodes\": [{\"distinct_partners\": 148, \"events\": 166, \"node\": 389}, {\"distinct_partners\": 114, \"events\": 132, \"node\": 987}, {\"distinct_partners\": 148, \"events\": 169, \"node\": 1299}, {\"distinct_partners\": 9, \"events\": 9, \"node\": 92}, {\"distinct_partners\": 41, \"events\": 41, \"node\": 1446}, {\"distinct_partners\": 40, \"events\": 43, \"node\": 1378}], \"window\": [5632, 44032]}", "latency_ms": 5, "tokens_before": 35684, "tokens_after": 35684, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_12", "tool": "neighbors", "args": {"node": 762, "direction": "out", "window": [5632, 44032]}, "result_digest": "6e9ae22c3811b564", "result_summary": "{\"direction\": \"out\", \"n_neighbors\": 17, \"neighbors\": [92, 268, 419, 553, 745, 856, 914, 1269, 1346, 1368, 1425, 1466, 1475, 1513, 1532, 1643, 1652], \"node\": 762, \"window\": [5632, 44032]}", "latency_ms": 1, "tokens_before": 46423, "tokens_after": 46423, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_13", "tool": "edges_between", "args": {"u": 762, "v": 1118, "window": [5632, 44032]}, "result_digest": "5a0dc944e934588a", "result_summary": "{\"connected\": false, \"n_events_u_to_v\": 0, \"n_events_v_to_u\": 0, \"u\": 762, \"v\": 1118, \"window\": [5632, 44032]}", "latency_ms": 0, "tokens_before": 46423, "tokens_after": 46423, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_2ea72f94", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [762, 1118], "window": [5632, 44032], "confidence": 0.91, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}], "narrative": "Under the 600-unit gap constraint, node 762 reaches 18 nodes and never 1118, with zero enumerable paths. Relaxing max_wait to 5000 and then to unbounded still fails to reach 1118 (26 and 28 nodes reached), showing the failure is structural time-ordering rather than excessive latency. A static, order-ignoring view is misleading here: the 2-hop neighbourhoods of 762 and 1118 share hubs 389, 987, 1299, 92, 1446 and 1378, so an atemporal analysis would report a connection. Those intermediaries are simply high-degree hubs (up to 148 partners), and overall volume is high (4,952 events, 1,880 active nodes), so neither sparsity nor lack of activity explains the result. The reverse direction reaches only 2 nodes, co-activity is low (Jaccard 0.125), and there is no direct edge. Conclusion: no genuine cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "## Conclusion\n\n**No time-respecting cascade from 762 to 1118 exists in this window.**\n\nKey findings:\n\n1. **Direct test fails** (step_01): With the 600-unit constraint, 762 reaches only 18 nodes; 1118 is not among them. No paths are enumerable (step_09).\n\n2. **The constraint is not the binding issue** \u2014 relaxing it disproves the \"just barely too slow\" explanation:\n   - `max_wait = 5000`: still unreachable, 26 nodes reached (step_10)\n   - `max_wait = \u221e` (no limit at all): **still unreachable**, 28 nodes reached (step_03)\n   \n   Since even unbounded waiting fails, the blockage is *directional/topological ordering*, not latency. The reachable set saturates at ~28 nodes regardless of patience.\n\n3. **Confounders controlled:**\n   - *Static connectivity*: The 2-hop neighborhoods genuinely overlap \u2014 389, 987, 1299, 92, 1446, 1378 appear in both (step_04, step_06). So an order-ignoring analysis **would** wrongly report a connection. The time ordering is what kills it.\n   - *Hub popularity*: Those shared intermediaries are high-degree hubs (389: 148 partners, 1299: 148, 987: 114 \u2014 step_11). Their prominence creates the illusion of a conduit but does not yield an ordered chain.\n   - *Volume*: 4,952 events over 1,880 active nodes (step_02) \u2014 ample activity, so absence is not from sparsity. Both endpoints are individually active (20 and 19 events, step_05).\n   - *Reverse direction*: 1118 \u2192 762 reaches only 2 nodes (step_07), confirming no cascade either way.\n   - *Co-activity*: Jaccard 0.125 (step_08) \u2014 the two are rarely even active in the same time bins.\n   - *Direct edge*: none in either direction (step_13).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_2ea72f94\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [762, 1118],\n  \"window\": [5632, 44032],\n  \"confidence\": 0.91,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Under the 600-unit gap constraint, node 762 reaches 18 nodes and never 1118, with zero enumerable paths. Relaxing max_wait to 5000 and then to unbounded still fails to reach 1118 (26 and 28 nodes reached), showing the failure is structural time-ordering rather than excessive latency. A static, order-ignoring view is misleading here: the 2-hop neighbourhoods of 762 and 1118 share hubs 389, 987, 1299, 92, 1446 and 1378, so an atemporal analysis would report a connection. Those intermediaries are simply high-degree hubs (up to 148 partners), and overall volume is high (4,952 events, 1,880 active nodes), so neither sparsity nor lack of activity explains the result. The reverse direction reaches only 2 nodes, co-activity is low (Jaccard 0.125), and there is no direct edge. Conclusion: no genuine cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 57617, "total_output_tokens": 3621, "total_tokens": 61238, "total_latency_ms": 50709, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}